  manifest and '/' path spelling.
- API-SPEC: 0.3.2 -- no method changes; on Windows paths come back with '/'
  and a drive root as C:/; ZWINROOT, else ZMACROOT (offline); Windows 10
  1903 or later.
- CAPTURE-ONE-CATALOG: "Capture One for Windows", from a throwaway 16.6.4
  catalog: the package as a plain folder with a writelock file, ZWINROOT
  and backslashes, ZPARENT -1, folder rows without a name, album groups,
  the colour-tag indices seen, and the snapshot copy under Windows' locks.
- DESIGN: NFC is done on Windows (NormalizeString); Linux stays identity.
- SESSION-DESIGN §6: partial answers to Q1-Q4 from a throwaway 16.6.4
  session on Windows (ZDOCUMENTTYPE 0, the role pointers on the root row,
  relative role folders, no writelock in the session folder, the .cos
