+**Findings so far (Capture One 16.6.4 for Windows, 2026-10-30).** A throwaway session `SpkProbe Session`
+(Blank template), three images imported into Capture, one rated 2, one rated 5 with the pink tag, an
+album holding one image; read from a byte copy of the db. These are partial answers; the
+verification script below is still the plan, and the read side waits for it.
+
+- Q1: `ZDOCUMENTTYPE` is **0** for the session (1 for a catalog) and `ZDOCUMENTUUID` is set. The
+  tables are the catalog's (21 of them). The four roles are not entities: the root `ProjectCollection`
+  points at them with `ZCAPTUREDESTINATIONLOCATION`, `ZSELECTSDESTINATIONLOCATION`,
+  `ZPROCESSDESTINATIONLOCATION` (Output) and `ZTRASHDESTINATIONLOCATION`, and at their folder rows
+  with `ZCAPTURECOLLECTION`, `ZPROCESSCOLLECTION` and `ZTRASHCOLLECTION`. Folders are
+  `FolderCollection` rows (`ZPARENT` -1, `ZNAME` NULL, one per role folder) whose membership *is*
+  stored in `ZIMAGEINCOLLECTION`; the Session Folders list is `SessionFolderCollection` rows; All
+  Images and "5 stars" are `SmartCollection` rows with criteria; albums are `AlbumCollection`.
+  Favorites were not created.
+- Q2: the role folders are `ZISRELATIVE = 1`, `ZRELATIVEPATH` `Capture`, `Selects`, `Output`,
+  `Trash`, `ZWINROOT` and `ZMACROOT` empty: relative to the session folder. A nested folder (to see
+  the separator) was not made.
+- Q3: on Windows no writelock file appears in the session folder while it is open (a catalog has
+  one in its package).
+- Q4: one `.cos` per image, `Capture/CaptureOne/Settings166/<file name>.cos`: XML, `<IMG>` with the
+  image's `UUID`, then one `<VAR>` per variant with the variant's `UUID`, a `<DL>` (adjustments) and
+  an `<AL>` holding `Basic_Rating` and `Color_Tag_Index` (absent when unset). The db holds the same
+  values on the combined layer. Previews are in `CaptureOne/Cache/Proxies` (`.cop`, `.cof`) and
+  `CaptureOne/Cache/Thumbnails` (`<file>.[<variant uuid>].cot`). Keywords and second variants were
+  not tried.
+- `capture_one.probe` on this session reports 3 images, 3 variants, 2 rated, 1 colour-tagged, which
+  is what Capture One shows; `capture_one.link` answers `unsupported`.
+
 **Verification script.** Run it in Capture One 16.8 on the owner's Mac with a **throwaway** session,
 never a real one. Every db read uses the snapshot procedure.
 
